Z||000000||sqoach||02-26-2001||10:02 PM||||started making one from fiberglass, but scratched the idea to try something else. i'm using fiberboard instead. found an old piece of an entertainment center and that's what i'm using. already have the speaker opening part cut out and shaped.<P>i'm also not having the speaker facing out. it's going to be hidden so nobody kicks it in. yeah, i could get a grill, but oh well.<P>stimpy, i still give you credit for some of this. the footwell is a good place.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig2.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)<p>[This message has been edited by sqoach (edited 02-26-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||AusFiero||02-27-2001||06:41 AM||||Are you sure the footwell is such a good idea?<BR>I just installed a 10" sub in a custom made console between the seats, replacing the original "glovebox". The new rear console section I made is only 3" deeper than the original console and is non obtrusive...and looks great with a red sony subwoofer installed there...the car is red too as is some of the custom upholstery.<BR>I also now have a more useable console section above the subwoofer and computer which is precisely 2 cd widths wide. <P>The console was made from MDF board which was screwed and glued then all joins got a blast from the hot glue gun to totally seal the unit..after upholstery and installation this has worked out to be a very practical, good looking solution to fitting a decent sub woofer into a Fiero.<P>Pictures will be online when I finish the rest of the interior...currently adding lots of Carbon Fibre..white face gauges and more.<P>Cheers<BR>Jim Davis<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||02-27-2001||10:14 AM||||Whatever works for you, guy. But since ou asked, here are my reasons to not go with a sub in the center console.<BR>1) At my size, bringing the face of the console up 3 inches would seriously impair my ability to drive the car, as I would not have full normal range of motion. Then again, I'm probably the largest person who can fit in a Fiero (6'6", 285 lbs) so maybe that's just me.<BR>2)Putting the sub up in plain sight like that is theif bait. Might as well leave a wallet with a couple of $100 sticking out.<BR>3)I don't like hacking up the interior of my car. I'm sure the results of your project came out fine. Mine was very easy,very reversible, and I am very happy with he results.<BR>4)Wouldn't having a big-ass woofer over the ECM tend to send some electro-magnetic fields that might not be so good for the ECM?<P>Not trying to piss on your parade, just stating why I feel the footwell is the best compromise for adding bass. You want no-comromise sound? Check out fierosound's install.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||02-27-2001||10:35 AM||||He moved the ECM behind the drivers seat, I think.  I'm doing the footwell because it's easier for me, and I actually use the psuedo-glove-box to keep stuff in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||william_thorniii||02-27-2001||11:34 AM||||Any of you sub folks interested in a slightly used Polk Dynamic Balance 10?  If so, lmk.  <P>THX,<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
Z||000005||Racer 1||02-27-2001||12:56 PM||||Back in the day I had made two 10" subwoofer boxes. The boxes were contoured to the back window and back behind the seat. I had like 1.3 cubic feet area for each box. Then I put a board going across to both boxes and mounted my amps on the board. Rockford Fosgate punch 200 powering kicker 10" subs sure was sweet. But driving room was hindered. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=159982&a=1168563&p=42189251&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||10
Z||000006||Racer 1||02-27-2001||12:58 PM||||Now im running one bazooka 8" sub infront of each seat. sounds awesome but not as loud as the 10" kickers. But alot more room and there hardly noticable when looking in.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=159982&a=1168563&p=42189251&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||14
Z||000007||Jimmy||02-27-2001||04:31 PM||||   About three years ago I used to have two 10" Fosgate punch subs behind the seats.  I then modified the boxes to fit two 12" cerwin vegas.  I have no idea what I was thinking, guess I just wanted to see if i could do it.<BR>   Oh BTW the seat was two notches from being all the way forward.  I'm 5'9" so not a big deal for me.  <BR>   If I do antoher sub box I think I am going to do a 12" behind the passanger seat.  The footwell does sound interesting though.  I've made my boxes out of MDF in the past, may try using fiberglass now. <P>Jim||||reg||1
Z||000008||sqoach||02-27-2001||06:10 PM||||this is a little tougher than i thought. i'm pretty good with this kind of stuff, but the angles are hard to match. i've only got the front and left part of the box. the top should be pretty easy, but the bottom/back/right of it is going to be tricky. maybe i'll use fiberglass to form those.<BR>i'll get some pics on here when i actually get somewhere with this.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||02-28-2001||12:18 AM||||I had enough trouble getting the construction paper to form there.. hehe.  Couldn't imagine trying to do it with fiberboard.  Good luck man!||||reg||1
Z||000010||AusFiero||02-28-2001||05:20 PM||||Yeah well I can imagine at your size stimpy putting yourself in a Fiero proves to be a challange every day. I am 5' 11" and am a tight fit.<P>The centre console application doesnt hinder anybody though...still have full arm travel etc.<P>Theft...well can't hide everything from em. If a car is going to be taken or broken into dual imobilisers and 2 alarm systems just doesnt stop em sometimes as I have found.<P>On to the computer issue.... The magnetic field cannot reach the ECM as it has 12 mm of mdf board and 6 mm of high density rubber between it and the back of the sub. Both are enclosed in their own insulated lined boxes basically...with vents for the computer to cool down.<P>But everyone has there own preferences on subs hey...seen a good installation behind the seats once...involved cutting out the inner firewall though. <P>And in closing..as I have never heard one...what is the peformance like on the factory subwoofers in Fieros? <P>Cheers<BR>Jim||||reg||6
Z||000011||stimpy||02-28-2001||11:25 PM||||Performance sound? Eh. Its's alright. Nice option to have if you just want a well optioned car that you want to keep stock. Gives about the same low end as a decent set of 6x9's in a sedan. Nothing to go hog-wild over though. I'd never consider adding it to a car. ||||reg||1
